US neurology residents and fellows in 2016. Neurology. 2017;89:492–501. doi: 10.1212/WNL.0000000000004135. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 37. O''Connor AB, Halvorsen AJ, Cmar JM, et al. Internal medicine residency program director burnout and program director turnover: results of a National Survey. Am J Med. 2019;132:252–261. doi: 10.1016/j.amjmed.2018.10.020. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 38. Mahajan A, Cahill C, Scharf E, Gupta S, Ahrens S, Joe E, et al. Neurology residency training in 2017: a survey of preparation, perspectives, and plans. Neurology. 2019;92:76–83. doi: 10.1212/WNL.0000000000006739. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 39. Vidaurre J, Campbell J. The case for an epilepsy and clinical neurophysiology match. Pediatr Neurol. 2017;72:5–6. doi: 10.1016/j.pediatrneurol.2017.04.017. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 40. The 2019 Executive Summary of the AAN Neurology Compensation and Productivity Report. https://www.aan.com/tools-and-resources/practicing-neurologists-administrators/benchmarking-data/neurology-compensation-productivity . Accessed November 15, 2020. 41. ACGME Program Requirements for Graduate Medical Education in Neurology. July 1, 2019. https://www.acgme.org/Portals/0/PFAssets/ProgramRequirements/180_Neurology_2019.pdf?ver=2019-06-18-132333-227 . Accessed December 2019. 42. Weber D, Sarva H, Weaver J, Wang F, Chou J, Cornes S, et al. Current state of educational compensation in academic neurology: results of a US national survey. Neurology. 2019;93:30–34. doi: 10.1212/WNL.0000000000007664. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 43. Applying to Fellowship Programs. https://students-residents.aamc.org/training-residency-fellowship/article/finding-and-applying-fellowship-programs-myeras/ . Accessed November 15, 2020. Associated Data This section collects any data citations, data availability statements, or supplementary materials included in this article. Data Availability Statement Not applicable.',1954,'2025-10-08 11:37