 racism: a theoretic framework and a gardener''s tale. Am J Public Health. 2000;90(8):1212-1215. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 13. Williams DR, Mohammed SA. Racism and health I: pathways and scientific evidence. Am Behav Sci. 2013;57(8):1152-1173. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 14. Saadi A, Himmelstein DU, Woolhandler S, Mejia NI. Racial disparities in neurologic health care access and utilization in the United States. Neurology. 2017;88(24):2268-2275. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 15. Robbins NM, Bernat JL. Minority representation in migraine treatment trials. Headache. 2017;57(3):525-533. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 16. Valenzuela F, Romero Arenas MA. An assessment of gender and racial/ethnic diversity amongst neurology residents and physicians (4918). Neurology. 2021;96(15 suppl):4918. [ Google Scholar ] 17. Charleston LT, Ovbiagele B. Diversity in neurology leadership: nuances and nudges. J Neurol Sci. 2021;426:117475. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 18. Yearby R. Race based medicine, colorblind disease: how racism in medicine harms us all. Am J Bioeth. 2021;21(2):19-27. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 19. Beauchamp TL, Childress JF. Principles of Biomedical Ethics. Oxford University Press; 2001. [ Google Scholar ] 20. Sandel MJ. Justice: What''s the Right Thing to Do? Farrar, Straus, and Giroux; 2009. [ Google Scholar ] 21. Rawls J. A Theory of Justice. Harvard University Press; 1971. [ Google Scholar ] 22. American Medical Association. AMA Code of Medical Ethics, Opinion 8.5. Disparities in Health Care; 2017. [ Google Scholar ] 23. Marulanda-Londoño ET, Bell MW, Hope OA, et al. Reducing neurodisparity: recommendations of the 2017 AAN diversity leadership program. Neurology. 2019;92(6):274-280. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 24. Vyas DA, Eisenstein LG, Jones DS. Hidden in plain sight—reconsidering the use of race correction in clinical algorithms. 