g clinical investigations in children’s endocrinology. Nurs Child Young People. 2015;278:26–36. quiz 7. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 22. Austin CP, Cutillo CM, Lau LPL, Jonker AH, Rath A, Julkowska D et al. Future of rare diseases research 2017–2027: an IRDiRC perspective. Clin Transl Sci. 2018;11[1]:21– 7. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] 23. Rizza RA, Vigersky RA, Rodbard HW, Ladenson PW, Young WF Jr., Surks MI et al. A model to determine workforce needs for endocrinologists in the United States until 2020. J Clin Endocrinol Metab. 2003;88[5]:1979-87. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] 24. Tsai K, Long C, Liang TZ, Napolitano J, Khawaja R, Leung AM. Driving factors to pursue endocrinology training fellowship: empirical survey data and future strategies. J Clin Endocrinol Metab. 2022;107(6):e2459–63. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 25. Allen DB, Aye T, Boney CM, Eugster EA, Misra M, Singer K, et al. Sustaining the pediatric endocrinology workforce: recommendations from the pediatric endocrine society workforce task force. J Pediatr. 2021;233:4–7. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 26. Freed GL, Boyer DM, Van KD, Macy ML, McCormick J, Leslie LK. Variation in Part-Time work among pediatric subspecialties. J Pediatr. 2018;195:263–8. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 27. Ocal G. Current concepts in disorders of sexual development. J Clin Res Pediatr Endocrinol. 2011;3(3):105–14. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 28. Hoe FM, Darbinian JA, Greenspan LC, Lo JC. Hemoglobin A1c and type 2 diabetes incidence among adolescents with overweight and obesity. JAMA Netw Open. 2024;7[1]:e2351322. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] 29. Illig R, Laron Z, Visser HK. From the paediatric endocrinology club to the European society for paediatric endocrinology: the early years of ESPE. Pediatr Endocrinol Rev. 2011;9[1]:417– 21. [ PubMed ] 30. Oberfield SE, Rogol AD, Miller WL. A brief history of the pediatric endocrine society [PES]. Horm Res Pae